# vocab/queries/adoption-candidate.rq
#
# THE ADOPTION GATE (spec 2026-08-09-adoption-at-document-scope §5.2, residue R73).
#
# Is this page's reading INCOMPLETE — does its holon carry an escalation? Both variables
# (?page, ?doc) are supplied by the caller as data; the query text carries no literal.
#
# WIDENED 2026-09-14 (R225 arm B, D2 — spec `2026-09-14-the-gate-not-the-predicate-design.md`).
# It used to ask whether the page was a TOTAL reading failure, by adding
#
#     FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?cell a tab:EntryCell ; tab:onPage ?page . }
#
# — one asserted cell anywhere on the page disqualified it. That absence test was an adequate
# proxy for "the bands failed" only while they failed totally: a page may hold a PARTIAL band
# reading and a COMPLETE grid reading at once, and the partial reading then excludes the complete
# one merely by existing (spec § 1c measures it on ons p7 — 94 asserted cells blocking a 276-cell
# reading). Absence is not the question; INSUFFICIENCY is.
#
# WHAT REPLACES IT IS NOT IN THIS QUERY, and that is deliberate. This gate runs on the PASS-1
# graph, before any grid exists, so it cannot compare the two readings at all — it can only ask
# whether there is anything to supersede. The comparison is an ordinal test on UNREAD INK and
# lives at the one site where both quantities are in hand (`compile.py`'s adoption branch, which
# refuses unless the grid leaves strictly less ink unread than the bands did). This query is now
# a CHEAP PRE-FILTER over a costly branch, never the adjudication.
#
# CLOSURE. Page scope is carried by the candidate's own SourceRegion (`iladub:onPage`) and by
# ?doc, the page-scoped document IRI every escalation on the page is derived from. With the
# NOT EXISTS gone this query closes over nothing at all: it is a pure positive pattern, open
# world throughout, and it DERIVES nothing — it only answers whether the document's last reader
# may be asked. (CLAUDE.md §8: recovery is open-world; the membrane is closed-world.)
PREFIX iladub: <https://w3id.org/iladub#>
PREFIX prov:   <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#>

ASK {
  ?candidate a iladub:CandidateConcept ;
             prov:wasDerivedFrom ?doc ;
             iladub:fromRegion ?region .
  ?region iladub:onPage ?page .
}
